.TH CUBIE-A7Z-FANCTL 8 "2026-10-19" "0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
cubie-a7z-fanctl \- temperature based hwmon PWM fan controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cubie-a7z-fanctl
.RB [ --config " PATH"]
.RB [ --check-config " | " --once ]
.br
.B cubie-a7z-fanctl
.RB [ --help " | " --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controls a PWM fan using the first valid configured temperature sensor.
Without a one-shot option, the program runs continuously.
Missing sensors select the configured fail-safe speed. Missing PWM devices
are periodically rediscovered. SIGINT and SIGTERM request a shutdown PWM
write when shutdown_pwm is configured.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read TOML configuration from PATH. The default is
/etc/cubie-a7z-fanctl/config.toml.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate configuration without accessing hardware.
.TP
.B --once
Perform one cycle and retain its PWM value. Missing temperature uses fail-safe;
missing PWM or failed writes cause a nonzero exit status.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.PP
The check-config and once options are mutually exclusive. Help and version
must be used alone and do not load configuration. Unknown, duplicate or
conflicting arguments cause a nonzero exit status.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The installed defaults target Cubie A7Z: hwmon name pwmfan, temperature
zones 0 and 3, with fallback disabled.
Device numbering is discovered automatically.
All fields in the example configuration are required except shutdown_pwm.
Unknown fields are rejected. Configured temperature bounds are in degrees
Celsius. Sensor readings are integer millidegrees Celsius in the range
-40000 to 150000; the first valid configured sensor is used.
PWM values are integers from 0 to 255; intervals are positive integer seconds.
Configuration is loaded at startup; restart the service after editing it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Invalid arguments or configuration, failed one-shot
control, or a failed requested shutdown write return a nonzero status.
Hardware errors in continuous mode are logged and retried.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/cubie-a7z-fanctl/config.toml
.SH SAFETY
Fallback PWM devices may control unrelated hardware. Verify device identity.
The program only inspects pwm1_enable; it never changes that attribute.
Omit shutdown_pwm to disable shutdown writes; TOML has no null value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
